  41:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****   \page CMSIS_MISRA_Exceptions  MISRA-C:2004 Compliance Exceptions
  42:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****   CMSIS violates the following MISRA-C:2004 rules:
  43:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h **** 
  44:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****    \li Required Rule 8.5, object/function definition in header file.<br>
  45:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****      Function definitions in header files are used to allow 'inlining'.
  46:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h **** 
  47:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****    \li Required Rule 18.4, declaration of union type or object of union type: '{...}'.<br>
  48:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****      Unions are used for effective representation of core registers.
  49:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h **** 
  50:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****    \li Advisory Rule 19.7, Function-like macro defined.<br>
  51:../../../../library/CMSIS/Include/core_cm0plus.h ****      Function-like macros are used to allow more efficient code.
